From b2b89db2c8bd45b6e1e4c2558e1a5aecc2ff991d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:33:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] PS1-RAM: the build warns under the 72 KB plan gate; a
 RAM ledger tool and the CI summary

ps1/tools/elf2exe.py prints the exact bytes left below the stack top and a
WARNING (a GitHub annotation on CI) when they are under the 72 KB plan gate,
long before the hard failure at 64 KB. The line the show engine reads keeps
its shape.

ps1/tools/ram_ledger.py reads the linker map: the layout (resident .text,
.rodata, .data, .bss, the borrowed .bss, the overlay slot, the margin), the
biggest resident objects with code / const data / strings / .bss apart, the
overlay groups by name and, with readelf, the biggest resident symbols. The
PS1 job writes it to the job summary.

ps1/tools/test_tools.py: unit tests of both (made-up ELF and map), run by CI.

Baseline on this machine (89a28b56, boot FMV linked): 65,936 B below the
stack top.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
