From d11456b86c637067838ab07cbd02aa2cde1e096a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:57:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] PS1-RAM step 6: shared core files give their one-group
 parts to that group (+18,448 B)

A core file outside the planner's GROUPS was resident as a whole, the parts
only one screen family calls included. For the files named in SHARED
(fishcook, catalog, ui, song_player, fp_common, audio, art_data_ps1,
mus_core) every .text / .rodata section is now a candidate like a group's
own: resident when resident code or data reach it or its address escapes;
when the scenes of exactly one group reach it, it joins that group; reached
by two groups it stays resident. A scene defined in such a file is a
resident scene. SHARED_NOT (story, home, combat, free play) take none: they
set the slot's size or are within a few KB of it.

Moved: the fishing / cooking effects and unlock checks (fishcook.c, 5.6 KB,
which also frees the fish and recipe tables it alone read: the fishcook
group 93 -> 101 KB), the creator's option names (catalog.c, 4.0 KB), the
paint picker and slider only the UI gallery draws (ui.c, 2.5 KB), the
island's ticker and HUD (fp_common.c, 2.0 KB), the studio's song helpers
(song_player.c, 1.6 KB). The linker script lists a shared file's sections
per group (one file can feed several groups). No source file changes.

Game disc with the boot FMV: 142,912 -> 161,360 B below the stack top.

test_tools.py: a shared file in the made-up game (one group, two groups,
the platform, its own scene, a group that takes none).

