Subject: [PATCH 10/11] PS1-RAM: a host test of the image cache's tile rows;
 the smoke run checks the boot-time SPU load

Step 5 writes a cached tile's bordered rows straight into the upload packets.
The row writer is now ps1/src/tilerow.h (tile_row, inlined into upload_rows:
the same code), and ps1/harness/tilerow_test.c compares it on the host with
the staging code it replaced, for full, narrow and short tiles, plain and
mirrored. The `harness` targets and the CI PS1 job run it.

Step 4 converts every effect at boot with buffers taken from the idle display
lists. The boot line now reads "spu: N of N effects (all), top ..., sum ..."
and game_smoke.txt expects "effects (all)": a conversion that found no
buffer would fail the smoke run instead of leaving the game silent.

Game disc with the boot FMV: 161,312 B below the stack top (48 B of text for
the log line).

