From 06f6f90452a65e0b89130c851b2194ae7b09265b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:36:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] PS1-RAM step 7: the groups on the hub's path take
 nothing new (HOLD)

What a group takes out of resident RAM is read with it from then on: about
2 ms of its load per KB at the drive's 2x speed. Measured on PCSX-Redux
with everything moved (161,312 B below the stack top): free play loaded in
340 ms instead of 314, the island in 226 instead of 206, the cutscenes in
355 instead of 348, and the two load windows of the speed tour that hold
those reads were 0.4-0.9% slower (new island: 16.52 -> 16.45 fps, title to
New story: 8.54 -> 8.46). Every other window was unchanged.

ovl_plan.py HOLD names those three groups: the title and the free-play
screens, the island hub (the player crosses both all the time) and the
cutscenes. A held group takes nothing new: its callbacks of steps 1
(HELD_CALLBACKS; they stay in their reviewed tables) are resident, its
objects' table strings stay together, it takes no shared code. The three
groups are byte for byte as big as on 89a28b56 (106,248 / 58,324 /
118,768 B), so their loads are as long as before. Taking a group off HOLD
releases it: free play 13.5 KB, the island 13.1 KB, the cutscenes 3.7 KB.

Game disc with the boot FMV: 131,312 B below the stack top (the 128 KiB of
the old goal is 131,072 B).

test_tools.py: a held group, a released one, a hold on the group next to
it, and that every held callback is in a reviewed table.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
